{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 4: the base of a landscape",
 "summary": "A 40 m plane subdivided 40 times turned into rolling hills with Set Position: the Position plus a Noise Texture's factor (scale 0.09) times a height Value (Math Multiply) on Z through Combine XYZ and Vector Math Add, and half the height subtracted (Math Divide, Vector Math Subtract) so the land stays at zero; Set Shade Smooth; Distribute Points on Faces (Poisson disk, minimum distance) with Instance on Points of small cubes as placeholders, joined with the land. Beyond the tutorial: last chapter's fence dropped onto the hills with a Raycast.",
